{"id":"0e800aa519680c23","group":"58","path":"58/batch08/58-df-manifold.md","title":"Manifold","display":"df-manifold — Manifold","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-manifold","aliases":["58-df-manifold","Manifold"],"display":"df-manifold — Manifold","depends_on":["[[../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md]]","[[../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md]]","[[../batch03/58-df-euclidean-topological-data.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-manifold"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-manifold</span><span>Manifold</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-manifold — Manifold"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c4b4a825f2ea608d\" href=\"?note=c4b4a825f2ea608d\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md\">../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"815e63e5071e7b58\" href=\"?note=815e63e5071e7b58\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ca7fc3ab38a11801\" href=\"?note=ca7fc3ab38a11801\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-euclidean-topological-data.md\">../batch03/58-df-euclidean-topological-data.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,\\tau\\in V\\land n\\in\\omega\">\\(M,\\tau\\in V\\land n\\in\\omega\\)</span> (carrier, topology, and dimension)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (topological-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"815e63e5071e7b58\" href=\"?note=815e63e5071e7b58\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Homeo}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\mathrm{Homeo}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span> (homeomorphism predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"c4b4a825f2ea608d\" href=\"?note=c4b4a825f2ea608d\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md\">../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}=\\mathrm{EuclideanSubspaceTopology}_S(\\mathbb R^n,n)\">\\(\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}=\\mathrm{EuclideanSubspaceTopology}_S(\\mathbb R^n,n)\\)</span>（欧氏拓扑的显式公式见内部依赖）。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Manifold}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Manifold}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (topological-manifold predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}manifold} \\vdash \\mathrm{Manifold}_S(M,\\tau,n) \\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(M,\\tau)\\land\\forall x,y\\in M\\;\\left(x\\neq y\\to\\exists U,V\\in\\tau\\;(x\\in U\\land y\\in V\\land U\\cap V=\\varnothing)\\right)\\land\\exists\\mathcal B\\subseteq\\tau\\;\\left(|\\mathcal B|\\leq\\aleph_0\\land\\forall U\\in\\tau\\;\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists B\\in\\mathcal B\\;(x\\in B\\subseteq U)\\right)\\land\\forall p\\in M\\;\\exists U\\in\\tau\\;\\exists V\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\\;\\exists\\phi\\;\\left(p\\in U\\land\\mathrm{Homeo}_S(\\phi,U,\\{W\\cap U:W\\in\\tau\\},V,\\{W\\cap V:W\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\\})\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}manifold} \\vdash \\mathrm{Manifold}_S(M,\\tau,n) \\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(M,\\tau)\\land\\forall x,y\\in M\\;\\left(x\\neq y\\to\\exists U,V\\in\\tau\\;(x\\in U\\land y\\in V\\land U\\cap V=\\varnothing)\\right)\\land\\exists\\mathcal B\\subseteq\\tau\\;\\left(|\\mathcal B|\\leq\\aleph_0\\land\\forall U\\in\\tau\\;\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists B\\in\\mathcal B\\;(x\\in B\\subseteq U)\\right)\\land\\forall p\\in M\\;\\exists U\\in\\tau\\;\\exists V\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\\;\\exists\\phi\\;\\left(p\\in U\\land\\mathrm{Homeo}_S(\\phi,U,\\{W\\cap U:W\\in\\tau\\},V,\\{W\\cap V:W\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\\})\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Manifold: locally Euclidean Hausdorff space</li>\n<li>Smooth: atlas with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C^\\infty\">\\(C^\\infty\\)</span> transition maps</li>\n<li>Dimension: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span> from local coordinate charts</li>\n<li>Tangent-space identifications such as <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T_pM\\cong\\mathbb{R}^n\">\\(T_pM\\cong\\mathbb{R}^n\\)</span> require smooth structure and are downstream from this topological definition.</li>\n<li>Examples: spheres <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S^n\">\\(S^n\\)</span>, tori <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{T}^n\">\\(\\mathbb{T}^n\\)</span>, projective spaces <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{RP}^n\">\\(\\mathbb{RP}^n\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Lee, Introduction to Smooth Manifolds</li>\n<li>Warner, Foundations of Differentiable Manifolds</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md","status":"resolved","id":"c4b4a825f2ea608d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-df-homeomorphism.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"